  triage:title "RULE-003 file-size ceiling exceeded in an in-diff file not covered by AW3-QA-B5: atm-http-runtime client.rs (1297 non-test lines)" ;
  triage:description "qa-pr1182-r3 (msg 01M1R214MSB951X2B06QCM5EA3, arch-qa) at db47e09c9: crates/atm-http-runtime/src/client.rs is at 1297 non-test lines (#[cfg(test)] mod tests boundary at line 1298 of 2108 total), against the 1000-line RULE-003 cap. quality-mgr independently confirmed via wc -l/grep, and confirmed the overage is pre-existing (already 1285 non-test lines / boundary at line 1286 of 2096 total back at the AW.3 round-1 tip 199a3bfeb) -- not introduced by the AW3-QA-B4/B5 fix round, but the file is touched in-diff this round (18 lines changed between 199a3bfeb and db47e09c9), so the zero-tolerance in-diff policy applies. This was not caught by the original AW3-QA-B5 sweep, which only named lib.rs and storage_and_nudge_router.rs. Fix: apply the same behavior-preserving module-extraction pattern used for AW3-QA-B5 to client.rs (e.g. split loopback/direct-peer/UDS client construction into separate files under src/), keeping the public re-export surface in lib.rs unchanged." ;
